WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.060
If a protein is enough to start making a motor neuron, does every motor neuron need

2
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:09.040
it?

3
00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:13.990
A factor is sufficient if adding it produces the effect, in the cells being tested.

4
00:00:14.983 --> 00:00:18.523
It is necessary there if the effect does not happen without it.

5
00:00:19.383 --> 00:00:22.083
Electroporation in chick tests sufficiency.

6
00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:24.823
Gene deletion in mouse tests necessity.

7
00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:32.163
In chick, Mnx1, or its relative MNR2, is enough to trigger motor-neuron

8
00:00:32.163 --> 00:00:33.163
differentiation.

9
00:00:34.017 --> 00:00:36.837
It also represses the neighbouring V2 programme.

10
00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:41.290
Predict. Delete Mnx1 in a mouse.

11
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.250
Are motor neurons made?

12
00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:45.130
Does anything go wrong?

13
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.320
They are made, on schedule and in normal numbers.

14
00:00:55.333 --> 00:00:58.113
But for a while they show V2 interneuron features.

15
00:00:59.053 --> 00:01:01.313
Their columns and axon paths are disordered.

16
00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:08.267
So Mnx1 is not needed to make a motor neuron.

17
00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:10.247
It is needed to keep one.

18
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.840
A motor neuron has to keep suppressing the interneuron programme.

19
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:16.700
That is the lock.

20
00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:21.440
Back up to the progenitors.

21
00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:26.280
Delete both Olig1 and Olig2, and motor neurons are largely lost.

22
00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:32.800
Lineage tracing suggested the progenitors make V2 interneurons, then astrocytes,

23
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:33.800
instead.

24
00:01:34.283 --> 00:01:38.003
Delete Isl1, and motor neurons are not generated at all.

25
00:01:38.967 --> 00:01:43.527
Now a puzzle. Delete Lhx3 and Lhx4.

26
00:01:44.607 --> 00:01:45.727
Motor neurons are still made.

27
00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:50.940
What changes is their subclass, and which way their axons leave the tube.

28
00:01:52.933 --> 00:01:56.073
Yet Lhx3 sits in the motor-neuron complex.

29
00:01:57.013 --> 00:01:58.113
How can both be true?

30
00:02:04.517 --> 00:02:06.277
The tests ask different questions.

31
00:02:07.257 --> 00:02:11.417
In chick, Isl1 plus Lhx3 is enough to start the programme.

32
00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:17.750
In mouse, motor neurons still form without Lhx3 and Lhx4, but of a different kind.

33
00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:20.710
Sufficient is not the same as necessary.

34
00:02:24.183 --> 00:02:27.303
Takeaway: enough, needed, and kept are different jobs.

35
00:02:28.163 --> 00:02:29.543
Each test answers only one.
